.TH TPM-FIDO 1 "2026-08-31" "tpm-fido" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tpm-fido \- virtual FIDO2 security key backed by TPM 2.0 and a fingerprint reader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpm-fido
.RB [ \-\-mode=\fImode\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-backend=\fIbackend\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-device=\fIpath\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-tray ]
.RB [ \-\-auto\-switch=\fIbool\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tpm-fido
is a FIDO2/WebAuthn authenticator for Linux. In daemon mode it creates a
virtual FIDO2 HID device through
.I /dev/uhid
that browsers use like a hardware security key.
.PP
Private keys are generated and stored in the TPM 2.0. User verification is
performed with the fingerprint reader through fprintd. The daemon runs in the
user session, so fingerprint verification and desktop notifications use the
logged-in user's own session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-mode= mode
Operating mode.
.B daemon
creates the virtual HID device.
.B native
runs as a Chrome Native Messaging host. The default is
.BR native .
.TP
.BI \-\-backend= backend
Signing backend.
.B tpm
uses the TPM.
.B memory
uses an in-memory key for testing only. The default is
.BR tpm .
.TP
.BI \-\-device= path
TPM device path. The default is
.IR /dev/tpmrm0 .
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Show a system tray icon for toggling the virtual device on and off. Daemon
mode only.
.TP
.BI \-\-auto\-switch= bool
Automatically disable the virtual key while a YubiKey is plugged in. Tray mode
only. The default is
.BR true .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/tpmrm0
TPM 2.0 resource manager device used for key operations.
.TP
.I /dev/uhid
Kernel interface used to create the virtual HID device.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tpm-fido/credentials.json
Resident credential metadata. Private keys remain in the TPM.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fprintd\-verify (1),
.BR fprintd\-enroll (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Peter Sanford and contributors.
